## The side drawer

Everything is reached from the drawer on the left. Its entries are grouped, and the groups always
appear in the same order:

| Group | What's inside |
| --- | --- |
| *(top level)* | Dashboard, What's New |
| **My Class** | Students, Attendance — a teacher's own class |
| **Students** | Student Search, Classes, Admissions, Prospectus, Fee Counter |
| **Attendance** | Summary, Reports, Saved Filters, Live Monitor |
| **Teachers** | Overview, Directory, Attendance, Substitution |
| **Timetable** | Timetable Grid, Class Subjects, Grade Curriculum, Configuration |
| **Exams** | Exams, Rankings, Result Changes, Progress Reports |
| **Analytics** | Overview, Students & Risk, Academics, Attendance, Payments, Operations |
| **Accounting** | Overview, Ledger, Manual Payment Entry, Online Payments, Day Close, Reconciliation, Fee Setup, Portal Access Rules, Invoices, Discounts |
| **Communication** | Send Messages, Notification History |
| **Administration** | Users, Locations, Settings, Access Control, Handbook, Prospectus, ID Cards, Holidays |
| *(head office)* | Group Overview, Branches, Teachers |
| **Reports** *(head office)* | Accounting, Analytics, Collections, Operations, Exams, Admissions, Demographics |
| **Configuration** *(head office)* | Discount Rules, Term Dates |

Teachers also get **My Timetable**, **My Attendance** and **My Profile** as their own top-level
entries rather than inside a group.

## Why your drawer looks different from a colleague's

The drawer is not a fixed menu. It is built from the screens **you** are allowed to open, so:

- A group you have no access to **does not appear at all** — it is not greyed out.
- A group you can only reach one screen in **collapses into a single tile**, without the expandable
  header. So "Timetable" may appear as a group for an admin and as a single **My Timetable** link
  for a teacher.
- Two people with the same job title can still see different menus, because access is granted per
  screen in **Administration → Access Control**, not per role.

If a screen this guide describes is missing from your drawer, that is an access question, not a bug.
Ask whoever administers your institute to check [Access Control](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-users-and-access).

## Getting back

The bar across the top shows breadcrumbs for where you are. Detail screens — a student profile, a
single exam class — highlight their **nearest parent** in the drawer rather than an entry of their
own, so the drawer stays put while you drill down.
